      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject code: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE\n- subject code description: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC\n- Political Science department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- degree-granting: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- number of students in each degree-granting department: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT\n- total number of students: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- school name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- average of the total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- range of the total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- variance of the total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- subjects offered in the 2022 academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- excluding 'Mathematics' departments: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT\n- department phone number: SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE <-> SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Political Science\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science'\"\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 17\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT = '18'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each subject code in the Political Science department, what is the subject code description and the geometric mean of the number of students in each department associated with that subject code, considering only departments that are degree granting?\n```sql\nSELECT s.SUBJECT_CODE, s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, EXP(AVG(LN(student_count))) AS geometric_mean_students FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON s.DEPARTMENT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN ( SELECT DEPARTMENT, COUNT(*) AS student_count FROM MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY GROUP BY DEPARTMENT ) m ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = m.DEPARTMENT WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science' GROUP BY s.SUBJECT_CODE, s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC ORDER BY geometric_mean_students DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, give the department name and calculate the average, range, and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year that are degree granting, but only include departments that are not 'Mathematics' (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, MAX(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ON SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER = SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <> '18' GROUP BY SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY total_units_range DESC;\n```\n3. For each subject code in the Political Science department, what is the subject code description, the geometric mean of the number of students in each department associated with that subject code (considering only degree-granting departments), and the total number of students across all such departments for each subject code? For each subject code, also include a grand total row with null for the subject code and description, and the total number of students.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT s.SUBJECT_CODE, s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, EXP(AVG(LN(student_count))) AS geometric_mean_students, SUM(student_count) AS total_students FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON s.DEPARTMENT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN ( SELECT DEPARTMENT, COUNT(*) AS student_count FROM MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY GROUP BY DEPARTMENT ) m ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = m.DEPARTMENT WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND d.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science' GROUP BY s.SUBJECT_CODE, s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC ) SELECT SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, geometric_mean_students, total_students FROM inner_cte GROUP BY SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, geometric_mean_students, total_students WITH ROLLUP HAVING SUM(total_students) > 0 ORDER BY SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC\n```\n4. For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, and calculate the average, range, and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year that are degree granting, but only include departments that are not 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, include the department phone number from the SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT table. Sort the results by school name and department name.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, MAX(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ON SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER = SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <> '18' GROUP BY SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.SCHOOL_NAME, icte.avg_total_units, icte.total_units_range, icte.total_units_variance, ad.DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER FROM inner_cte icte LEFT JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME = sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME LEFT JOIN SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT ad ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ad.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY sd.SCHOOL_NAME, icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each subject code in the Political Science department, what is the subject code, subject code description, the geometric mean of the number of students in each degree-granting department associated with that subject code, and the total number of students across all such departments for each subject code, along with, for each department and school associated with those subject codes, the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year that are degree granting (excluding 'Mathematics' departments), and the department phone number? Present the results ordered by subject code, school name, and department name. Do not return any rounded answers."
