      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"table_name\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"count\": 13, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_2272\", \"name\": \"Math Department Unit Statistics with Course Level Student Counts and Lecture-Lab Unit Averages\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4458\", \"name\": \"2009SP Status-U Reserve Materials Windowed Faculty Row Numbers with EECS Course Student Directory Details\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U' and term code '2009SP', show the course instructor key, reserve catalog key, subject offered key, the responsible faculty name, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the responsible faculty name from the associated subject offered, and for each matching course in the \\\"Electrical Eng & Computer Sci\\\" department, show the course description, course level, the full name and email address of students enrolled, and the row number within each course level group ordered by the student's last name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_100\", \"name\": \"Top 5 Departments by Graduate Student Average Office Phone with Highest-Phone Student\", \"category\": \"Student Directory Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Among all departments, which are the top 5 departments with the highest average office phone number among graduate students (student year 'G') who have a non-null office phone number? For each of these departments, show the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of office phone numbers, and the full name and office phone number of the graduate student in that department with the highest office phone number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_463\", \"name\": \"EECS Course-6 Students Min MIT ID and Average Department Number with Email\", \"category\": \"Person Master and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each student in the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department whose MIT ID is between 921145998 and 999756146 or whose department number is at least 4, and whose department number is between 4 and 6, and whose department number is 6, what are their minimum MIT ID, average department number, and email address? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1033\", \"name\": \"Math Graduate Students School Dense Ranks Unioned with Department CIP Code Range-Variance\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department name, department full name, student full name, student email address, dense rank over the school code, CIP program code range, and CIP program code variance for all graduate students in degree-granting Mathematics departments, as well as for all Mathematics departments that are degree granting and have at least one course with a non-null CIP program code, including the CIP program code range and variance for those departments even if they have no such students. List the results ordered by department full name and student full name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1212\", \"name\": \"Math Department Subject Unit Average-Stddev with Graduate Student Count and Latest Load Date\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1350\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department TIP Enrollment Statistics with School Rollups and Math Peter Student Budget Code Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1474\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Engineering Degree-Granting Department Subject Counts with Kevin EECS Student Course Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 degree-granting departments (excluding 'Political Science' and Course 17) that have offered at least one subject in the 'Engineering' school, list the department name, school name, subject code description, the total number of subjects they offered, and the average number of enrolled students per subject, and for each such department, show the full names, email addresses, student years, department full names, course descriptions, course levels, the minimum course level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's last name, and the corresponding subject code and subject code description for each course taken by students named 'Kevin' in 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' (Course 6). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1983\", \"name\": \"EECS Students Windowed Admin Department Phone Averages with Engineering Subject Load Categories\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For students whose department is '6' and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', show their first name, last name, department name, student year, the corresponding department's full name, the administrative department name, and the average department phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the administrative department name and ordered by the student's first name. Additionally, for each subject offered in the 'Engineering' school with total units greater than 0 and only for subjects in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department (Course 6), where the student's department matches the subject's offer department code, show the subject title, total units, subject department name, course description, and the dense rank over the offer department code ordered by offer department code. Finally, for each such subject, include the corresponding department's school name and whether the total units are 'HIGH_LOAD' (at least 12), 'LOW_LOAD' (at most 6), or 'MEDIUM_LOAD' (otherwise). Present the columns in the following order: first name, last name, department name, student year, department full name, administrative department name, average department phone number (windowed), subject title, total units, subject department name, course description, dense rank (windowed), department school name, and subject load category. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2240\", \"name\": \"EECS Engineering Subject Max Units and Distinct Student Year Counts per Offer Department\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 'Engineering' school with total units greater than 0 and only for subjects in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department (Course 6), show the subject title, total units, department name, course description, and dense rank over the offer department code ordered by offer department code, along with the first name, last name, department name, student year, corresponding department's full name, administrative department name, and the average department phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the administrative department name and ordered by the student's first name, for students whose department is '6' and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', where the subject's offer department code matches the student's department. Then, for each offer department code, provide the maximum total units among these subjects and the count of distinct student years among the matched students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2759\", \"name\": \"Graduate Student Employee Type Department Counts with Min MIT ID and Unique Office Locations\", \"category\": \"Person Master and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each employee type and department name where the student year is 'G', show the number of people, the minimum MIT ID, and the list of unique office locations for those employees. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3237\", \"name\": \"2021 Engineering Degree-Granting Department Subject Counts with Active Graduate Student Office Totals\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3969\", \"name\": \"2017JA Subject Enrollment Windows Matched with Above-Average-Last-Name EECS Student Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', and for students in the \\\"Electrical Eng & Computer Sci\\\" department whose last name is alphabetically after the average last name (in terms of ASCII value) within their course level group, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, the school name, department phone number, the student's full name, email address, department name, course description, course level, and the student's row number within their course level group ordered by last name. Order the results by subject code, course level, and student row number within course level. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
